			<div class="content" id="post-content-4836624">
									

<p>Yeah.</p>
<p>As was originally conceived, the Hand was a kind of exciting foil to the Foundation's dogma. The latter is this vast, unknowable, bureaucratic, militaristic, disingenuous, <em>evil</em> institution born from all the worst aspects of mankind intent of preserving the murderous status quo, and then comes the Hand — alien, unscientific, unorganized, pacifists. And the whole thing is couched in religious terminology — the Hand is the Serpent in the Garden of Eden, come to bring humanity forbidden knowledge and free them from the shackles of God. And it's&#8230; kind of cool. I'd like to be a magician.</p>
<p>But honestly, that's part of the reason that the Hand has fallen out of favor of late. We have the Wanderers' Library and all the lore that the introduction of the Hand helped cultivate, but generally, people seem more interested in exploring GOIs like AWCY and GAW over people who are just supposed to be &quot;good&quot;. I mean, I think the last time I heard people talking about the SH seriously was regarding <a href="/scattersomnia">Scattersomnia</a> — excellent read, you should check it out.</p>
<p>But yeah. Magic is cool. It's a nice sort of escape in a universe where the big players are doing it all wrong, and unlike GAW, they have a kind of force behind them, enough to stand up for themselves.</p>

