					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1918720&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607485206" alt="Scorpion451" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1918720)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;" >Scorpion451</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607233632 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2020 05:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837670">
									

<p>Food for thought counterpoints:</p>
<p>The Serpent's Hand can also be seen as an elitist, objectivist organization operating on the most dangerous interpretation of &quot;Do what you will.&quot; They operate on the assumption that their cause is righteous and inviolable, deriding and harassing any who oppose their unquestionable judgement. No locked door can ever be justified, no matter what lies on the other side. No cage can be justified, no matter what it holds back. Knowledge is free for anyone regardless of intent, except to those deemed unworthy- especially those who question any of the previous.</p>
<p>The Foundation is an organization of mortals, holding back a hostile universe through grit and wit. They have no illusions about their own ethics- They know that sometimes the right call is the lesser of two evils, and accept the consequences of that. They know that simply trying to find more than those two options can have consequences, and accept those as well. They aren't the knight in shining armor. But they aren't the wicked stepmother, either. They're the woodsman with the axe, and they're here to chat with this alleged grandma about where the kid in the red jacket went.</p>
<p>TL;DR: If you're looking for clear good guys and bad guys in the SCPverse, you're not going to find them.</p>

							</div>

								
					
