			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838159">
									

<blockquote>
<p>No locked door can ever be justified, no matter what lies on the other side. No cage can be justified, no matter what it holds back. Knowledge is free for anyone regardless of intent, except to those deemed unworthy- especially those who question any of the previous.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As I said before: S.H. isn't going around breaching highly dangerous euclids and keters just for the sake of it. They aren't stupid, and they don't want the end of the world. They just want knowledge of the paranormal to be out in the open and accessible, and also want equal rights for anomalous humans (<em>especially</em> reality benders). The Serpent's Hand <em>does</em> believe in the destruction or containment of highly dangerous anomalies, however. Also, the Serpent's Hand is not without their flaws, either. You are acting as if the Foundation has no flaws, as well.</p>
<p>Also, the SH deems everybody worthy of knowledge of the occult, so long as they use that knowledge for good.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The Foundation is an organization of mortals &#8230; They have no illusions about their own ethics- They know that sometimes the right call is the lesser of two evils, and accept the consequences of that.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Are you sure? I find locking people up simply because they are abnormal is pretty evil. Some of the anomalous humans in Foundation containment haven't even done anything wrong.</p>

